- How would you leverage __builtin_popcountll if available?
- How would you generalize to 256-bit types?

## Why This Is Asked
Tests ability to count 1-runs in a 64-bit word using bit-twiddling with no loops.

## Key Concepts
- Start mask n & ~(n << 1) identifies 1-run starts
- Parallel popcount technique to count bits
- Edge cases: all zeros, runs spanning MSB

## Code Example
```cpp
uint64_t countOneRuns64(uint64_t n){
  uint64_t starts = n & ~(n << 1);
  uint64_t x = starts;
  x = x - ((x >> 1) & 0x5555555555555555ULL);
  x = (x & 0x3333333333333333ULL) + ((x >> 2) & 0x3333333333333333ULL);
  x = (x + (x >> 4)) & 0x0F0F0F0F0F0F0F0FULL;
  return (x * 0x0101010101010101ULL) >> 56;
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you adapt for 128-bit operands?
- Compare this approach to a loop-based scan in terms of latency and pipeline efficiency.

## Why This Is Asked

Tests knowledge of bitwise compression patterns and correct use of masks. Avoids loops and relies on proven parallel bit extraction tactics.

## Key Concepts
- compact1by1 technique
- masks and shifts for bit packing
- 64→32-bit narrowing without branches

## Code Example

```javascript
// Signature example (conceptual):
uint32_t packEvenBits64(uint64_t x) {
  x &= 0x5555555555555555ULL;
  x = (x | (x>>1)) & 0x3333333333333333ULL;
  x = (x | (x>>2)) & 0x0F0F0F0F0F0F0F0FULL;
  x = (x | (x>>4)) & 0x00FF00FF00FF00FFULL;
  x = (x | (x>>8)) & 0x0000FFFF0000FFFFULL;
  return (uint32_t)(x | (x>>16));
}
```

## Why This Is Asked
Tests ability to reason about 128 bit manipulations and zero edge cases without branching.

## Key Concepts
- Branchless bit tricks
- 128 bit layout as hi and lo
- De Bruijn based ctz for 64 and 32 bit values
- Handling zero input gracefully

## Code Example
```c
typedef struct { uint64_t hi; uint64_t lo; } uint128;

static inline int ctz64(uint64_t x) {
  if (x == 0) return 64;
  static const int tab[64] = { /* 64 entries */ };
  uint64_t y = x & -x;
  return tab[(y * 0x03f79d71b4cb0a89ULL) >> 58];
}

int lsbIndex128(uint128 x) {
  uint64_t lo = x.lo, hi = x.hi;
  int a = ctz64(lo);
  int b = 64 + ctz64(hi);
  int m = - (int)(lo != 0);
  int res = (a & m) | (b & ~m);
  return (lo | hi) == 0 ? -1 : res;
}
```

